# Frontend Architecture - React/TypeScript

## Routing

Brepia uses TanStack Router with React Start. Do not introduce React Router patterns.

- `src/router.tsx` creates the router.
- File-based routes live in `src/routes/`.
- `src/routes/__root.tsx` owns the root document and route-level head content.
- Layout routes live under `src/routes/_layout*`.
- Server API routes live under `src/routes/api/`.
- `src/routeTree.gen.ts` is generated by TanStack Router and must not be edited manually.

Route files should stay thin where practical: route registration and request/view wiring belong there, while reusable UI belongs in components/views and reusable server logic belongs in `src/server/`.

## Components and views

- Page-oriented implementations live primarily in `src/views/`.
- Reusable UI lives in `src/components/`, organized by feature/domain.
- Base UI primitives live in `src/components/ui/` and follow the existing shadcn/Radix patterns.
- Preserve accessibility attributes, keyboard behavior and responsive layouts when changing existing UI.
- Prefer existing shared components and feature patterns over adding parallel abstractions.

## State and data access

- React Query is used for server state, caching and invalidation.
- React Context is used for appropriate shared client state such as authentication and appearance.
- Local component state should remain local unless it genuinely needs shared ownership.
- Follow existing service/hooks for data access. Some flows use Supabase directly while application-server functionality uses `/api/...` routes; do not assume every request is a Supabase call.
- Authenticated Brepia API calls should reuse the existing authenticated API helpers/patterns rather than hand-rolling bearer-token handling in components.

## 3D and OpenSCAD

- Three.js and React Three Fiber provide browser 3D rendering.
- OpenSCAD compilation uses the existing worker/WASM integration.
- Preserve cleanup, WebGL-loss handling, model lifecycle and stable-runtime behavior when modifying viewer or generation code.
- Do not change Parametric or Creative behavior as an incidental UI refactor.

## Styling

- Tailwind CSS and existing shadcn/Radix primitives are the default styling system.
- `src/index.css`, `src/appearance.css` and `tailwind.config.js` contain shared styling/theme behavior.
- Existing `adam-*` Tailwind/CSS tokens are compatibility-sensitive. Do not rename them as cosmetic cleanup.
- Reuse Brepia brand components/assets instead of recreating product marks in feature code.

## Error and loading states

- Preserve route/component error boundaries and existing toast/error patterns.
- Show explicit loading, empty and failure states for asynchronous UI.
- Do not swallow server errors or silently substitute different providers/models.

## Generated and shared files

- Never hand-edit `src/routeTree.gen.ts`.
- Prefer shared types from `shared/` or existing domain types over duplicating API shapes locally.